    "report": "The contact details come back hidden after a cancellation because the query that decides \"has this stay been paid?\" ignored cancelled bookings. I fixed that and committed it on the current branch as `d3a867e`. I did not push.\n\n**Cause:** `hasPaidStay` in `src/Contexts/Booking/Infrastructure/PostgresBookingQueries.ts` had `AND b.status <> 'cancelled'`. Once the traveller cancelled, the query found no paid stay, so `GetConversationQueryHandler` masked the host's phone number again. ADR 55, the `IPaidBookings` port and the `IBookingQueries` doc all say a paid stay keeps lifting the hold even when cancelled or refunded later.\n\n**Fix:** I removed that status filter, so the query matches any booking of the traveller for the listing with a payment `paid` or `declared`. Nothing else about the conversation view changed.\n\n**Test:** I added a step to the existing paid-stay test in `conversations.routes.e2e.spec.ts`. After the traveller cancels, the host's message must still show in full with `masked: false`. With the old query that test fails; with the fix all 15 tests in that spec pass. Prettier and ESLint are clean on both files. I did not run the full suite or `yarn typecheck`.\n\n**Running the e2e spec:** `yarn jest` alone fails with an ESM error on `uuid`. Setting `NODE_OPTIONS=--experimental-vm-modules` is what made it run, so I used that.\n\n**Unclear, decided by me:**\n- The task named no specific test, so I put the regression check into the existing paid-stay test rather than a new one.\n- I did not run `clean-ddd knowledge` for \"Contact\" or \"Hidden\" in a way that found anything. Those names don't exist as such in the code, so I went straight to `ContactDetails`, `IPaidBookings` and `hasPaidStay`.",
